# reel's web demo: google.com, driven in Chromium over DevTools. `mise run demos google` records it. (WebKit, the
# default, draws Google's page blank: it paints little while reel, a command line tool, is not the active app.)
Import //demos/reel.reelpreset
Open https://www.google.com

Output //docs/media/google.mp4
Output //docs/media/google.gif
Set Browser chromium
# What fits under a browser's title bar on a 1080 point high screen.
Set Viewport 1280x720
# reel's own stings open and close it, as they do the Musicbox demo; the square cut gets title cards.
Intro@crossfade,ease-out,600ms square ? "reel" "Web pages too" : 2s
Outro@fade,800ms square ? "Recorded with reel" "brew install --cask mpdreamz/tap/reel" : 2s

# Every take starts in a fresh browser, so Google asks about cookies every time: answered off camera.
Hide
Click "Reject all"
Wait "Search"
Show
Caption "Open a page, type, press return"
Click "Search"
Type@70ms "demo videos of mac apps"
Key return
Sleep 2s
Caption "Typed and searched: no Accessibility, your mouse stays yours"
Sleep 3s
